{:edb/db-before-t 2549 :edb/db-after-t 2550 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535862 50 #inst "2026-10-15T02:10:47.858Z" 13194139535862 17592186045443 true] [17592186092263 1038 #edb/ref 17592186534162 13194139535862 17592186045443 true] [17592186092263 1038 #edb/ref 17592186534163 13194139535862 17592186045443 true] [17592186092263 1038 #edb/ref 17592186534167 13194139535862 17592186045443 true] [17592186092263 1038 #edb/ref 17592186534168 13194139535862 17592186045443 true] [17592186092263 1038 #edb/ref 17592186534173 13194139535862 17592186045443 true] [17592186092263 1040 #edb/ref 17592186534177 13194139535862 17592186045443 true] [17592186534162 1068 #edb/ref 17592186534166 13194139535862 17592186045443 true] [17592186534162 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535862 17592186045443 true] [17592186534162 1071 "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y=e^{-2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-1}$ at the point where $x=2.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535862 17592186045443 true] [17592186534162 1072 #uuid "07e0afd0-4729-561c-85c0-8bd11d965ce5" 13194139535862 17592186045443 true] [17592186534162 1074 "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=e^{u},\\,u=-2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=e^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-6{x}^{2}+6x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ & =e^{u}\\cdot (-6{x}^{2}+6x) \\\\ & =(-6{x}^{2}+6x)e^{u} \\\\ & =\\left(- 6 x^{2} + 6 x\\right) e^{- 2 x^{3} + 3 x^{2} - 1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=2$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|_{x=2} & =(-6{x}^{2}+6x)e^{-2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-1}|_{x=2} \\\\ & =(-6(2)^{2}+6(2))e^{-2(2)^{3}+3(2)^{2}-1} \\\\ & =-12\\cdot e^{-5} \\\\ & =- \\frac{12}{e^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535862 17592186045443 true] [17592186534163 1068 #edb/ref 17592186534176 13194139535862 17592186045443 true] [17592186534163 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535862 17592186045443 true] [17592186534163 1071 "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y=e^{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-1}$ at the point where $x=2.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535862 17592186045443 true] [17592186534163 1072 #uuid "0be68eb4-fee3-576f-ac3a-d663b1b8b84c" 13194139535862 17592186045443 true] [17592186534163 1074 "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=e^{u},\\,u={x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=e^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}-4x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ & =e^{u}\\cdot (3{x}^{2}-4x) \\\\ & =(3{x}^{2}-4x)e^{u} \\\\ & =\\left(3 x^{2} - 4 x\\right) e^{x^{3} - 2 x^{2} - 1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=2$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|_{x=2} & =(3{x}^{2}-4x)e^{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-1}|_{x=2} \\\\ & =(3(2)^{2}-4(2))e^{(2)^{3}-2(2)^{2}-1} \\\\ & =4\\cdot e^{-1} \\\\ & =\\frac{4}{e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535862 17592186045443 true] [17592186534164 1075 #edb/ref 17592186534172 13194139535862 17592186045443 true] [17592186534164 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139535862 17592186045443 true] [17592186534164 1077 "field-1" 13194139535862 17592186045443 true] [17592186534164 1078 #edb/ref 17592186534172 13194139535862 17592186045443 true] [17592186534164 1079 #uuid "1f0c0cc9-ce45-5282-a4db-796430d6adf7" 13194139535862 17592186045443 true] [17592186534165 1080 "- 4 e" 13194139535862 17592186045443 true] [17592186534165 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535862 17592186045443 true] [175